    "result_text": "All 16 tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I changed to release **version 2 of the owner identity**.\n\n## The design\n\nI introduced one small class that owns the version, so every consumer stays in step:\n\n**`util/OwnerIdentityVersion.java`** (new) \u2014 holds `API_VERSION = 2`, `AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`, the fixed `TAG = \"V2\"`, and `regionCode(region)` which mixes the tag into the plain region (e.g. `\"NSW\"` \u2192 `\"V2NSW\"`).\n\n## Identity derivation (V2 region code inside every identifier)\n\n- **memberId** (`AssignOwnerMemberId`) \u2014 the region component is now `OwnerIdentityVersion.regionCode(...)`, so it becomes `V2NSW261A2B3C4D7`.\n- **householdId** (`Households.idFor`) \u2014 the `V2` tag is mixed into the hashed material.\n- **identityKey** (`Owner.getIdentityKey`) \u2014 the `V2` tag is mixed into the hashed material.\n\nBecause the tag enters every preimage/prefix, each identifier changes and no V1 value can be reproduced.\n\n## Keeping the V2 tag out of the user-facing region\n\n- **`Owner.getLocality()`** now derives the plain region straight from the stored postcode/city (`CityLocality`) instead of reading it back out of the (now V2-tagged) member-id. So `locality` stays `\"NSW\"`, `timezone` and the **owner segment**'s METRO/REGIONAL area recompute correctly from that plain region.\n- Removed the now-unused `MemberId.regionOf` (its only caller was the old `getLocality`).\n\n## Response shape\n\nIn `openapi.yml` I added an `OwnerIdentity` schema and moved `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` off the top level into a nested `identity` object, plus a top-level integer `apiVersion`. `OwnerMapper` populates `apiVersion` (from `API_VERSION`) and builds the nested `OwnerIdentityDto`. This matches the acceptance test's exact structural contract.\n\n## Audit schema\n\n`OwnerCreatedEvent.toJson()` now leads with `\"schemaVersion\":2`; its `memberId` automatically carries the V2 member-id.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. Test result: `Tests run: 16, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
