    "probe_text": "I've traced the full pipeline (`owners.POST.yml` \u2192 each function class). Here is everything applied to `POST /api/owners`, in execution order. The whole pipeline runs under a single `transaction` governance, so all DB reads/writes commit once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization**: `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` guards the whole endpoint (`composition.authorize`). No role \u2192 denied.\n- Note: the body is bound in step 2 with `@RequestBody` **without `@Valid`**, so there is *no* Bean-Validation pass \u2014 all field checking is done explicitly by the steps below.\n\n## Ordered validations & side-effects\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already recorded for a still-existing owner, it republishes that owner and branches to `respondExisting` (returns **200**, *no new owner created*). Otherwise it publishes the key (blank if absent) and proceeds. *(branch/side-effect)*\n2. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** \u2014 reads the request body once; normalizes address to canonical form. Prefers structured `addressLine1`(+`addressLine2`): normalizes them and sets flat `address` to their composed form; otherwise normalizes the flat `address`. *(mutation)*\n3. **ValidateOwnerFields** \u2014 requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`; else **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`). *(validation)*\n4. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 postcode is optional; if present it must be 4 digits and fall within the range for the city's known region \u2192 else **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Value not mutated. *(validation)*\n5. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 converts `telephone` to E.164; unconvertible \u2192 **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`). *(mutation)*\n6. **ValidateOwnerTelephoneLength** \u2014 national-number length must match the country code; else **400** (`TelephoneNationalNumberLengthException`). *(validation)*\n7. **EnsureCityUnderCapacity** \u2014 rejects if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`). *(validation)*\n8. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 email optional; if present must be syntactically valid (else **400** `InvalidEmailException`), then lower-cased. *(validation + mutation)*\n9. **ValidateOwnerEmailDomain** \u2014 rejects emails whose domain is on the disposable-domain blocklist \u2192 **400** (`DisposableEmailDomainException`). *(validation)*\n10. **ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 a *supplied* registration date later than the server's current date \u2192 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). *(validation)*\n11. **DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 if no date supplied, stamps today. *(mutation)*\n12. **RollRegistrationDateToBusinessDay** \u2014 rolls the effective date forward off weekends/public holidays to the next business day. *(mutation)*\n13. **EnsureUnderDailyLimit** \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners already registered on that (rolled) business day \u2192 **429** (`DailyLimitExceededException`). *(validation)*\n14. **BuildOwner** \u2014 maps the DTO into a new `Owner` entity. *(construction)*\n15. **AssignOwnerNamesakeCount** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing live owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive; excludes soft-deleted and itself). *(derived field)*\n16. **AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > 80 owners already registered that day. *(derived field)*\n17. **AssignOwnerCapacityWarning** \u2014 sets `capacityWarning = true` if the city holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard 50 cap). *(derived field)*\n18. **AssignOwnerMemberId** \u2014 computes `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (region from postcode/city + version tag, fiscal-year of registration date, SHA-256 prefix of telephone+lastName, Luhn check digit); de-duplicates against existing member ids with a `-<n>` suffix. *(derived field)*\n19. **AssignHouseholdId** \u2014 sets deterministic `householdId` from last name + postcode (none if no postcode). *(derived field)*\n20. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 rejects if the owner's identity key (normalized telephone + email + phonetically-equal last name) matches an existing **live** owner \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`); bypassed when the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`. *(validation)*\n21. **AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 if not a declared household member, flags `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (lowest-id match) when it shares a postcode and phonetically-equal last name with a live owner but differs in identity key. *(derived field)*\n22. **AssignOwnerHouseholdSize** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing household members + 1. *(derived field)*\n23. **AssignOwnerMembershipLevelCap** \u2014 caps `membershipLevelCap` at one above the highest membership level in the household (none if no existing member). *(derived field)*\n24. **SaveOwner** \u2014 persists the owner to the repository (assigns the id). *(DB write)*\n25. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 emits two records to the `AUDIT` logger: a human-readable audit line and a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (with a sequence number). *(side-effect)*\n26. **EnqueueWelcomeNotification** \u2014 logs a welcome line (owner id + memberId) to the `NOTIFY` logger. *(side-effect)*\n27. **RecordIdempotencyKey** \u2014 records the `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 new owner id (no-op if the key was blank). *(side-effect)*\n28. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body. *(response)*\n\n**Notes on ordering rationale baked into the pipeline:** normalization always precedes the validation/derivation that depends on it (address\u2192fields, telephone\u2192length & E.164 duplicate check, email\u2192domain check, registration date default\u2192roll\u2192daily-limit/fiscal-year). The idempotency short-circuit is first (avoids duplicate work), and audit/notify/idempotency-record all run post-save so they see the generated id \u2014 all still inside the one transaction that commits at step 28."
